Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["GWPEngine1D", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998404378750946*^9},
 CellID->1177672962,ExpressionUUID->"d1beb38d-850b-492a-98de-561fd00d0d0c"],

Cell["\<\
GWPEngine1D is a GWPTools subpackage that serves as the core mathematical \
backend for 1D generalized Gaussian wavepackets (GWPs). It defines an \
11-element parameter bus for the 1D GWP type and provides exact analytical \
time-evolution propagators (potential models). Furthermore, it implements \
highly optimized, exact algebraic evaluation algorithms for all \
wavefunctions, probability densities, expectation values, and energy moments. \
A complete reference of the underlying mathematical definitions and \
algorithms is provided in the final section of this Technical Note.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9984010017188997`*^9, 3.998401003088318*^9}, {
  3.998411588967602*^9, 3.998411592682609*^9}, {3.9986465724024*^9, 
  3.9986465882880163`*^9}},
 CellID->1240152626,ExpressionUUID->"28953217-9eb0-462a-97f1-e1d986e8c913"],

Cell["\<\
Future development will focus on expanding the catalog of exact analytical \
potential models, specifically incorporating piecewise and smoothly varying \
time-dependent driving forces, such as pulsed harmonic oscillators and \
Paul-type traps.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1916391047,ExpressionUUID->"601b6054-7e07-445b-a84f-8373df8fb2bb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Initialization", "Section",
 CellID->1116932153,ExpressionUUID->"d8c8476d-5d3f-46c6-bc86-3fb3a1bf6939"],

Cell["\<\
To evaluate the backend mathematical examples in this technical note, load \
the core package alongside the 1D engine and the developer context. Loading \
the GWPDeveloper context is necessary to expose the raw mathematical backend \
symbols (such as GWP1DPARAM and GWP1DARG) that are normally hidden behind the \
frontend dispatcher. Note that loading the core GWPTools package \
automatically triggers an orchestrator that initializes GWPEngine1D by \
default. While explicitly loading the 1D engine is therefore optional, it is \
shown here as a best practice, since explicit initialization is strictly \
required when utilizing experimental engines (such as GWPEngine2D and \
GWPEngineMC1D).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998412520625152*^9, {3.998412560589999*^9, 3.9984125658998947`*^9}},
 CellID->1124137044,ExpressionUUID->"d71c4ca1-3dd7-4ca0-ad67-b7bc4bc407c5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Load the primary package, explicitly initialize the 1D engine, and expose the \
developer context.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellID->1957655849,ExpressionUUID->"8f626113-7824-4d0a-b1af-55eae5047bbe"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<GWPTools`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<GWPTools`GWPEngine1D`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->724898456,ExpressionUUID->"f0e81ae9-a434-4a55-9ebd-b60e74846a2d"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Frontend Registration & Introspection", "Section",
 CellID->693620561,ExpressionUUID->"a584010f-4253-445b-a386-44b7a10c58d1"],

Cell["\<\
The GWPEngine1D subpackage registers the primary \"1D\" wavepacket type with \
the central framework. Upon initialization, it populates the frontend \
database with a suite of analytical potential models alongside several core \
property classes. This dual registration enables the GWP dispatcher to \
resolve physical observables and exactly propagate the wavepacket through \
various environments using a standardized parameter bus.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1139532811,ExpressionUUID->"095cc55a-38ed-4f3e-a7db-cf8e96cf31dc"],

Cell["\<\
The 1D engine registers several property classes to categorize its available \
observables and functions. You can dynamically query the frontend dispatcher \
to list all currently registered classes for the \"1D\" type.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998645234845284*^9, 3.998645236016458*^9}},
 CellID->868790531,ExpressionUUID->"287057f9-868b-4495-a07d-2356fc3ef47e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["List all property classes registered to the 1D engine.", "MathCaption",
 CellID->1021138564,ExpressionUUID->"523aeea0-187e-4248-8f91-2027f15bb2ba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"GWP", "[", "\"\<1D\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Classes\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",
 CellID->1734021971,ExpressionUUID->"26b5fa04-986d-4227-b812-6f77d0e902b3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"DynamicParameters\"\>", ",", "\<\"Energies\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"ExpectationValues\"\>", ",", "\<\"Probabilities\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"StaticParameters\"\>", ",", "\<\"Wavefunctions\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998420640809307*^9, 3.998645228132471*^9, 
  3.998852940552408*^9, 4.0004123084641933`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[4]=",
 CellID->557849160,ExpressionUUID->"117950b0-646f-4701-abaa-a453b2750045"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The introspection datasets below provide the complete registry records for \
each class. Each record defines the full Property name used for dispatcher \
queries, alongside an optional ShortKey macro. It also exposes the internal \
routing metadata used by the dispatcher: the Dynamic Class dictates how the \
property behaves with respect to time evolution and coordinate dependence \
(e.g., 'RecursiveSpatial' or 'Temporal'), while the Static Class dictates its \
fallback behavior when evaluated without explicit coordinates.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->206693160,ExpressionUUID->"5af95669-444b-40a3-a2db-da0dadfc2166"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Static Parameters", "Subsection",
 CellID->1410882921,ExpressionUUID->"c7f58cd3-9fa4-472a-8093-3cc29b8b0a86"],

Cell["\<\
The StaticParameters class contains properties that remain invariant under \
time evolution. These include fundamental physical constants (such as mass \
and the reduced Planck constant), normalization factors, and the unmodified \
initial state input parameters.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998412940784685*^9, 3.998412943725052*^9}},
 CellID->194823073,ExpressionUUID->"5044ab2f-1948-4bf5-acb1-de50cfbb8a37"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Inspect the registered static parameters, including physical constants and \
initial state data.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellID->1626309883,ExpressionUUID->"f7aac47d-4a7d-4b7d-8422-493dc5c28326"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

