Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Backend Mathematical Engines (Developer)", "Section",
 CellID->1770100650,ExpressionUUID->"fcddbc2c-b9d1-4ab6-837e-d43149f5b15d"],

Cell["\<\
The underlying backend functions utilize raw mathematical symbols to ensure \
maximum evaluation speed. The 1D math engine uses an 11-element parameter bus \
to represent the wavepacket's internal kinematics and local environment. \
Functions leverage a curried signature architecture to separate \
hyperparameters (like derivative order or potential frequency) from the \
evaluation coordinates and parameters.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->990662659,ExpressionUUID->"495b7ddf-21f0-4535-a5bc-9c8c24f03745"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Parameter Bus (GWP1DARG & GWP1DVAL)", "Subsection",
 CellID->626594622,ExpressionUUID->"6fbcba79-7bf3-48b5-83b6-8d32476f0420"],

Cell["\<\
The symbols GWP1DARG and GWP1DVAL are core developer macros representing the \
1D parameter bus sequence. GWP1DARG is used as a pattern sequence to define \
function signatures, while GWP1DVAL is a sequence of symbols used to pass the \
evaluated parameter bus seamlessly into other backend functions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2063490713,ExpressionUUID->"30e1b831-c6b6-4182-a296-64d19174ba61"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the developer macros to view the exact 11-element symbolic sequence \
used for function signatures (ARG) and internal variable routing (VAL).\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellID->1374997988,ExpressionUUID->"3e2c9f9f-e5b5-494f-aacf-5d32943637b5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{"GWP1DARG", "\n", "GWP1DVAL"}], "Input",
